      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="chawkins, SRI, caspi">Thiocoraline is a thiodepsipeptide antitumor compound produced by two actinomycetes (|FRAME: ORG-6291| and |FRAME: TAX-349725|) that were isolated from two marine invertebrates (a soft coral and a mollusc) found at the Indian Ocean coast of Mozambique. Ithas promising antitumor activity |CITS: [16408310]|.</Comment>
